---
description: How to set this repo up, and what to do with the keys it needs
alwaysApply: true
---

This repo is a daily competitor-alerting bot that runs on GitHub Actions. It
does nothing until its keys are set.

On a fresh clone, fork, or first session in this repo, run
`npm run check-env -- --strict` and read the output. It names every missing
variable, what it is for, and where the value comes from. Then prompt the user
for each missing value, one at a time, and have them stored as **GitHub Actions
secrets** – `gh secret set <NAME>`, which prompts without echoing, or Settings →
Secrets and variables → Actions. `SLACK_CHANNEL_ID` and `AGENTMAIL_INBOX_ID` are
Actions variables rather than secrets. A local `.env` is for local runs only.

Never ask for a secret value to be pasted into chat, never write one into a file
or a commit, and never print one in a log or a summary. Refer to secrets by
name. If a value lands in your context by accident, say so and tell the user to
rotate it.

[AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) has the full setup flow and the house rules for
changing anything here – in particular that all copy follows PostHog's docs
style guide, which means en dashes and never em dashes.
